<section class="app-measure-section" aria-labelledby="progress-rwm-heading">
    <h2 class="govuk-heading-m" id="progress-rwm-heading" data-testid="progress-rwm-heading">Progress score in reading, writing and maths</h2>
    <details class="govuk-details app-measure-details" data-module="govuk-details">
        <summary class="govuk-details__summary">
            <span class="govuk-details__summary-text">Information about progress score in reading, writing and maths</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="govuk-details__text">
            <p class="govuk-body-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
                The progress score shows how much progress pupils made in reading, writing and maths between the end
                of key stage 1 and the end of key stage 2, compared to other pupils across England with similar prior attainment.
            </p>
            <p class="govuk-body-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-2">
                The score shows progress compared to the national average:
            </p>
            <ul class="govuk-list govuk-list--bullet govuk-!-font-size-16 govuk-!-margin-bottom-2 app-measure-copy-list">
                <li>a score of 0 means pupils in this school made similar progress to others with similar starting points</li>
                <li>a score of above 0 means pupils made more progress than average</li>
                <li>a score of below 0 means pupils made less progress than average</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="govuk-body-s govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
                The confidence interval gives a range of scores the school could have achieved based on the cohort of pupils and natural variation in pupil performance across England.
            </p>
        </div>
    </details>

    <div class="app-measure-message-panel">
        <p class="govuk-body govuk-!-margin-bottom-0">
            There are no KS1-KS2 progress scores for the academic years 2023/24 and 2024/25, as there is no KS1 baseline available due to COVID-19 disruption.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
